STORED PROCEDURE;

One-Line Definition

A Stored Procedure is a precompiled and reusable set of 
SQL statements stored in the database that can be executed by calling its name.


SYNTAX:




CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE PROCEDURE_NAME( [ PARAMETER1 DATATYPE ],[ PARAMETER2 DATATYPE ],,,,N)
RETURNS DATATYPE
LANGUAGE SQL
AS
$$

[  DECLARE
     VARIABLE1 DATATYPE;
     VARIABLE2 DATATYPE;  ]
    
BEGIN

    -- SQL Statements

    RETURN VALUE;

END;
$$;




CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE HELLO()
RETURNS VARCHAR
LANGUAGE SQL
AS
$$
BEGIN
    RETURN 'HELLO HOW R U';
END;
$$;


CALL HELLO();








